\"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","signer_pubkey":null},{"content_hash":"7eb9e53e84034839c8e156411fce6b234274253a26e14a48dd6080ab76f3174c","event_uuid":"cc04c173-61f0-41b2-b6d8-d6facc821bb9","position":{"commit_sha":"89b8589222d556a70375107a3288022653dfa482","position":"1795082068001582659-cc04c173-61f0-41b2-b6d8-d6facc821bb9"},"signature":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","signer_pubkey":null},{"content_hash":"8b5cb98d8cc0f95784ff5b5352f8680f721493cde99c44ef464e8b3a4c073c87","event_uuid":"86bdc9a3-15d5-469a-b7a4-b069e676ca12","position":{"commit_sha":"a662e99c0a099702e6bb3a9f2d100afe357651ec","position":"1795082105256780650-86bdc9a3-15d5-469a-b7a4-b069e676ca12"},"signature":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","signer_pubkey":null},{"content_hash":"d7bde71b6324dc8ef70d8cfc74b77078371e1657e2a368da03cdced6af1f4f51","event_uuid":"d54d76ef-6ef8-4976-95b6-83e60e698666","position":{"commit_sha":"680984b24fbf6bc34abcfa8b2c41c810d3547fa8","position":"1795082211545485159-d54d76ef-6ef8-4976-95b6-83e60e698666"},"signature":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","signer_pubkey":null},{"content_hash":"0374f89d9ae935c137ce6a00247d950bd4e6d31b9ee9d922e5843eb3d422b676","event_uuid":"4b71c2a3-8dbb-4918-8d6d-061bbf79c189","position":{"commit_sha":"204d08eb790ba8d8c4cef1271099c37dd115b842","position":"1795082215983226838-4b71c2a3-8dbb-4918-8d6d-061bbf79c189"},"signature":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","signer_pubkey":null}],"bridge_alerts":[],"bridge_project":null,"claim_harness":null,"claim_remote_session":null,"claimed_session":null,"comments":[{"author":"Rebar Bot","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","body":"## Operator decision (2026-11-18): option (3), document reliance on the default ACL\n\nOn Windows, rebar does not enforce signing-key confidentiality itself. The POSIX mode-bit check is skipped on Windows, and keys rely on the user profile's default ACL, which normally grants the owner, SYSTEM and BUILTIN\\Administrators. The residual risk is documented. The same applies to the artifact-directory check in infra/scripts/cleanup_comment_echo_jira.py.\n\nRejected: (1) an OpenSSH-style owner-only DACL check plus a protected DACL on key copies; (2) declaring the op-cert service and the cleanup script Linux-only, failing closed.\n\nImplementation is in almondy-columned-iguanodon:\n- Skip only where the platform has no POSIX mode bits (os.name == \"nt\"). Keep the check unchanged everywhere else, and name the reason in the skip.\n- Record the residual risk in the docs: on Windows, keys inherit their folder's ACL; `chmod` changes only the read-only bit; there is no check on extra ACEs (for example Users or Everyone).\n- To meet this ticket's acceptance criterion, capture `icacls` output for a freshly minted signing key on a Windows runner and record it in a comment here.","timestamp":1795051416997695453},{"author":"Rebar Bot","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","body":"Acceptance evidence: `icacls` of a freshly minted op-cert signing key on a Windows runner. Source: Windows sweep run 44456347985, job 135332660982 (main at ab323f7df0c, 2026-11-19 04:11 UTC; 2026-11-18 20:11 PST), step \"Print the ACL of a freshly minted op-cert key\", which mints the key with rebar's own generator (`rebar._opcert_signing._generate_opcert_key`, i.e. `ssh-keygen -t ed25519` into a staging dir, then published by link).\n\nKey folder `D:\\a\\_temp/opcert-acl-probe` (inherited):\n```\nBUILTIN\\Administrators:(I)(F)\nBUILTIN\\Administrators:(I)(OI)(CI)(IO)(F)\nNT AUTHORITY\\SYSTEM:(I)(F)\nNT AUTHORITY\\SYSTEM:(I)(OI)(CI)(IO)(F)\nNT AUTHORITY\\Authenticated Users:(I)(M)\nNT AUTHORITY\\Authenticated Users:(I)(OI)(CI)(IO)(M)\nBUILTIN\\Users:(I)(RX)\nBUILTIN\\Users:(I)(OI)(CI)(IO)(GR,GE)\n```\nFreshly minted key `...\\opcert-acl-probe\\.opcert-key`:\n```\nBUILTIN\\Administrators:(F)\nNT AUTHORITY\\SYSTEM:(F)\nrunnervmm7ud1\\runneradmin:(M)\n```\nA fresh `tempfile.mkdtemp()` directory (where `keyprov.compose_signer` writes its key copy):\n```\nNT AUTHORITY\\SYSTEM:(OI)(CI)(F)\nBUILTIN\\Administrators:(OI)(CI)(F)\nOWNER RIGHTS:(OI)(CI)(F)\n```\nReading: the minted key carries explicit, non-inherited entries for only Administrators, SYSTEM and the owner, so it does not inherit the folder's Users / Authenticated Users access. That restriction comes from `ssh-keygen`, not from rebar. A key provisioned through `REBAR_OPCERT_KEY_PATH` gets whatever ACL the operator gave it, which is the residual risk now documented in `docs/manifest-signing.md` (merged in ab323f7df0c, Gerrit 3440).\n\nDecision (operator, 2026-11-18): option (3), rely on the default ACL and document the residual risk. Implemented by almondy-columned-iguanodon.","timestamp":1795066877402712898}],"completion_expectation":"required","created_at":1792886204914654001,"creation_channel":"cli","deps":[{"link_uuid":"0215728f-4df7-4bce-8a42-fc9b1fe904e2","relation":"discovered_from","target_id":"5f44-63ed-5428-4da0"},{"link_uuid":"abd9aa49-5656-490a-9b69-ab57f4e44f6b","relation":"relates_to","target_id":"44b2-e70e-2b9f-4d2a"},{"link_uuid":"13d49f05-a32c-496d-898d-45977ff37272","relation":"relates_to","target_id":"977f-11fe-1dcb-4b7d"}],"description":"## Context\nBug 5f44-63ed-5428-4da0 made the signing-key mode test skip where the platform does not honour POSIX permission bits. On Windows the key reports mode 0o666 because Windows does not implement POSIX bits, so the 0o600 guarantee the test checks on POSIX is not checked there at all.\n\n## Approach\nDecide whether rebar must restrict the op-cert signing key's access on Windows (an ACL limited to the owner) or document that Windows relies on the user profile's default ACLs. If the former, scope the implementation as a separate change with a Windows-runner test.\n\n## Testing\nInspect the effective ACL of a freshly minted signing key on a Windows runner (icacls output recorded on the ticket); no code change for the decision itself.\n\n## Acceptance Criteria\n- [x] The decision (restrict via ACL, or document the default) is recorded on this ticket with the observed Windows ACL of a new signing key (checked: icacls output in a ticket comment).\n","env_id":"492a5c71-6cda-48a6-8134-02ff6a672739","file_impact":[],"file_impact_scope":"none","keyring":[],"last_status_env_id":"eea68b7f-6697-488b-ac52-744e2ed8e96f","managed_refs":[["relates_to","44b2-e70e-2b9f-4d2a"],["relates_to","977f-11fe-1dcb-4b7d"]],"no_file_impact_reason":"Why no repository files change: this task records a policy decision and Windows-runner ACL evidence; the code and docs that implement the decision change under almondy-columned-iguanodon. Where output or evidence lives: the operator decision and the icacls output are comments on this ticket (icacls from Windows sweep run 44456347985, job 135332660982).","parent_id":null,"parent_status_uuid":"d54d76ef-6ef8-4976-95b6-83e60e698666","plan_review_phase":"execution","preconditions_summary":{"status":"pre-manifest"},"priority":3,"releases":[],"repos":[],"reverts":[],"status":"closed","tags":["security","windows","signing"],"ticket_id":"47d8-baf8-2348-45c9","ticket_type":"task","title":"Decide whether rebar owes Windows signing-key confidentiality (ACL equivalent)","verify_commands":[]},"source_event_uuids":["abd9aa49-5656-490a-9b69-ab57f4e44f6b","975afadc-756d-4997-ab36-f638134818d8","13d49f05-a32c-496d-898d-45977ff37272","e4f82124-780e-4860-95a3